# Pin line endings in the REPOSITORY, so they do not depend on each machine.
#
# Measured 8 September 2026: every text blob in the index is already LF
# (345 i/lf, 0 i/crlf, 0 i/mixed), so this pins what is already true and
# renormalises nothing.
#
# The exposure this closes is NOT the working tree on a Windows machine with
# core.autocrlf=true — there git converts on checkout and back on staging, so
# CRLF never reaches a blob. It is a machine WITHOUT that setting: a CI runner,
# a Mac, a colleague with a default install. There, editing any file would
# commit CRLF and produce a diff touching hundreds of files that hides the real
# change inside it.
#
# text=auto lets git decide what is text; eol=lf fixes what text looks like in
# the working tree and in the blob.
* text=auto eol=lf
